STRING CATALOG
  5 of the 14 keys already existed in res/values/strings.xml (translation_Scheduled, translation_Unknown,
  translation_Vehicle, translation_error_loadFailed, translation_softwareUpdates_title). The 9 web inline-default
  literal keys were absent, so they were added — to the canonical web i18n source (web/src/i18n/en.json) AND to the
  generated res/values{,-ar,-he}/strings.xml (an allowed file) with the verbatim web default values:
    translation_Current_Version, translation_Updates_Installed, translation_Total_Updates, translation_Update_Timeline,
    translation_Software_Updates, translation_View_release_notes, translation_No_update_history,
    translation_No_software_update_history_available, translation_Track_firmware_versions_and_update_history.
  The status-chip labels reuse the existing translation_widget_softwareUpdate_status* keys (Installed / Installing /
  Downloading / Available / scheduled), whose values are identical to the web STATUS_CONFIG labels; they are not
  among the 14 required parity strings.
  IMPORTANT (no silent drift) — `gen-i18n.ts --check` reports the repo's i18n catalog was ALREADY drifted before this
  change (web en.json leaves=8096 grouped=8062 vs the committed strings.xml header translated=7781, 11 files), a
  PRE-EXISTING condition unrelated to this page. Re-running the full generator would balloon the diff across all 11
  platform files (android/apple/windows × en/ar/he + catalog); per the artifact's allowed-files scope, the 9 keys
  were added surgically to en.json (canonical, so a future regen reproduces them) + the three android strings.xml
  catalogs only. ar/he ship as full English fallback, so the mirrors carry the English value (matching the generator).

